      "value": "<p>Eleven household hearths spread over four kilometres of wind shadow behind a basalt ridge, each with its own stone screen and none of them walled. The whole cluster is dismantled and refounded a few hundred metres nightward roughly once a generation, following the habitable band. Abandoned hearth positions run back from the current cluster in a line, and can be counted.</p>",
